   "start": 0.32,
   "text": "To absorb all this, you need surface, circular folds, the valvulae conniventes. Triple the area. Villi multiply it ten times more. Each epithelial cell adds a brush border of up to a thousand microvilli. Twenty fold again. Together, that's about 600 times. Roughly 250 square meters, the size of a tennis court. And the biggest contributor? The microvilli."
  }
 ],
